// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL8_Boyd_Compound1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - SuppliesBoyd 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P4287609718" "Scientific Supplies"
// DetailString :
"P625586277" "You were given this box of scientific supplies by Dr. Bruce Boyd to deliver to Dr. Ada Huxley"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3542832859" "There are just dozens of things that need to be done, {HeroName}, but I suppose one of the first things that needs your attention actually isn't for me. I have a collegue who's stationed deeper within the Shadow Shard. Her name is Dr. Ada Huxley, and her work is getting stalled due to a lack of supplies. Could you do me a great favor and get some scientific supplies to her?"
// AcceptString :
"P721514054" "Get Scientific Supplies to Dr. Ada Huxley"
// SendOffString :
"P2524276384" "Excellent, excellent! Now, she's stationed in the Cascades, the next known region of the Shadow Shard. In order to reach her you're going to need to use a Hortha Vine. Just in case you haven't done that before, I've called ahead and asked Lt. Quinn Volkov to give you a quick orientation. Speak with him first, then he'll send you along to Dr. Huxley."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL8_Boyd_Compound1_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3156741257" "Speak with Lt. Volkov"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P227667298" "You should speak with Lt. Volkov. He can tell you all about the Hortha Vines."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2682777942" "Okay, {HeroName}, I don't know if you've used a Hortha Vine before, but just in case, let me give you the basics. Those big purple tubes you see here and there are Hortha Vines. Hortha Vines are some kind of living conduit through time and space. At the most basic level, you step in one end, and step out somewhere else. The science types talk a lot about breaking causality and 5th dimensional evolution and get all excited, but really, the important thing is that they take you from place to place, and they're relatively safe. <br><br>Now, the woman you're looking for is Dr. Ada Huxley. She's in a hidden base we have in the Cascades called 'Mole Point Charlie'."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL8_Boyd_Compound1_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1029629293" "Find Dr. Huxley"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2634672305" "Lt. Volkov should have told you how to use a Hortha Vine. They're fascinating things. I could go on for hours the possibility of 5th dimensional evolution and they way they could disrupt causality, but Dr. Huxley needs those supplies."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1348605150" "Are these the supplies from Dr. Boyd? Thank you... <br><br>Oh, wow! <br>I'm sorry, {HeroName}, I didn't realize it was, well, you. Well, um, let me just say it's a real delight to get these, uh, scientific supplies from you. Thank you for coming all this way. <br><br>I don't know if you've been briefed on it yet, but the teleporter here could make your return trip much shorter. Why don't you ask Lt. Col. Flynn about it?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL8_Boyd_Compound1_Part3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2999173152" "Speak with Lt. Col. Flynn"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2285490965" "You did get some orientation on how to use the Mole point teleporter from Lt. Col. Flynn, didn't you?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1464280451" "Hey, there, {HeroName}. Ada asked me to make sure you'd been breifed on how to use the teleporter here in Mole Point Charlie. It's real easy. We've been trying to set up these secret 'Mole Point' installations whereever we can, to provide safe bases to explore the Shadow Shard. After we lost contact with Mole Point Bravo, we set up a teleportation system to link them, in case we have to evacuate. <br><br>In order to access a new Mole Point, you'll have to calibrate it by talking to the Mole Point Operator. Once you've spoken to a Mole Point Operator, he'll activate the Mole Point teleporter for you and you'll be able to access it from any other Mole Point you've used before. <br>Since we only have two set up right now, this one will only take you right back to Mole Point Alpha inside Firebase Zulu. Speak with the Mole Point Operator and give it a go."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL8_Boyd_Compound1_Part4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P373439036" "Speak with Mole Point Operator"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1960105952" "Lt. Col. Flynn should have told you to speak with the Mole Point Operator. That should make return trips much easier."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1559315289" "Glad you're here, {HeroName}. Now that I've calibrated the Mole Point teleporter to your pattern, you'll be able to use the teleporter here at Mole Point Charlie to go to Mole Point Alpha in Firebase Zulu whenever you want. You'll also be able to  use the teleporter there to return here. <br><br>As we get deeper into the Shadow Shard, we may be able to add more Mole Points. But right now, Alpha and Charlie are all we have. Give it a try."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskBegin 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2440335848" "You get some scientific supplies from Dr. Boyd."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3897525887" "Thank you ever so much, {HeroName}. Dr. Huxley's already told me that her work's back on track, thanks to you."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL8_Boyd_Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - MonumentRecords 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1009137781" "Monument Record"
// DetailString :
"P1677755169" "You recorded these pictures and measurements of a hidden monument in the area around Firebase Zulu for Dr. Bruce Boyd."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2694112353" "We've received a report of a hidden monument deep in one of the nearby caves. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>Getting a good set of records and photographs of that monument would be extremely useful</A>, but my own people can't get in there, owing to an infestation of Rularuu. General Hammond isn't willing to risk a mission just for archeological purposes, so I thought perhaps I could ask you?"
// AcceptString :
"P1994200272" "Take recordings of a hidden monument"
// SendOffString :
"P1422772191" "Thank you so much, {HeroName}. I'm glad that you're willing to help on this. As I mentioned, there are Rularuu infesting the caverns where the monument is located, but defeating them is by no means an imperative."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3203328793" "Find Monument"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P167794453" "Just get some detailed records and photos of the monument for me. Don't worry about risking your life or anything."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P2191682927" "The Rularuu are definitely here. You wonder if the monument you're looking for will be guarded."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Monument 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
